## Paid-user launch gate (blocks first paid users)

- GitHub delivery: deployed adapter/webhook verification against the production PR-artifact flow; deeper issue/linking polish.
- Task timeline: deployed UI/API verification of `task → A2A → runtime events → artifact → PR → preview → approval` against real paid-user data.
- CloudEvent outbox: production enablement + NATS JetStream verification on the deployed stack.
- Instruction provenance: deployed UI verification of compiled InstructionBundle artifacts.
- Runtime evidence: deployed runtime-adapter coverage for real sandbox sessions across every paid-user runtime.
- MCP approval loop: deployed PM verification against real MCP tool calls.
- Live edge/preview rollout: DNS, TLS, protected preview hosts, rate limits, WAF hooks, production verification (`recoder-zvss`).
- Hetzner deploy hygiene: reconcile local↔prod git divergence so full deploys don't need scoped checkout/build handling (`recoder-js56`).
- Production traffic/abuse controls: real-traffic threshold tuning + production alert review (`recoder-a9rp`, `recoder-rbc2`).

## Security / hardening

- [recoder-0zso] `/api/a2a/*` auth — broad per-route enforcement on the legacy task + workspace *mutating* routes that internal services (agency/agents/pm) currently call without auth headers. Needs an internal-service-key auth path + full product-loop runtime verification before enforcing. `.well-known/agent.json` stays public by spec.

## Capability layer — follow-ups (prod, infra access required)

- Bring up Qdrant + ziti on prod (NOT Ollama/vLLM — 16GB/no-GPU box); set cloud LLM + Gemini keys per `docker-backend/.env.capabilities.recoder-server`.
- Stand up OpenZiti controller end-to-end + provision a runner (`scripts/provision-ziti-runner.sh`); needs CA trust (`NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`).
- Free prod disk (94% used; 135GB is vcpeer — do not touch) before enabling capability backends.

